Every opioid-first-taper-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
Every benzodiazepine-first-taper-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
Every full-agonist-opioid-buprenorphine-transition-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
If a patient receives an opioid at a current-opioid-dosage and receives a benzodiazepine at a current-benzodiazepine-dosage and a risk outweighs a benefit during a continued-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-therapy then every clinician should individualize a medication-taper-sequencing-decision for the patient and should reevaluate a medication-taper-sequencing-decision during a regular-follow-up.
